@dev Implementation of the {IERC165} interface.
Contracts that want to implement ERC-165 should inherit from this contract and override {supportsInterface} to check
for the additional interface id that will be supported. For example:
```solidity
function supportsInterface(bytes4 interfaceId) public view virtual override returns (bool) {
    return interfaceId == type(MyInterface).interfaceId || super.supportsInterface(interfaceId);
}
```

@title EvidenceCommitment
@dev Commitments H_E = Hash(Evidence) to off-chain evidence, scoped PER INCIDENT.
     Keyed by (incidentId, evidenceHash) so nobody can claim a hash under a wrong incident.
     ResponseProposal requires at least one commitment before a response can be proposed.

@title FederatedVoting
@dev Commit-reveal voting among the eligible (affected) domains.
     Commitment = keccak256(chainId, this, proposalId, voter, choice, salt)  (replay-safe).
     Governance parameters are snapshotted at voting start.

@title GovernanceParams
@dev Federation-wide parameters. Values are snapshotted by the consuming contracts
     at the start of a vote / correlation so changes never affect in-flight decisions.

@dev Called by the contract responsible for the stalled phase:
     proposal contract (RESPONSE_PROPOSED expired), decision contract (VOTING, no quorum),
     execution contract (EXECUTING past its deadline).

@title ResponseExecution
@dev Execution plan for an APPROVED proposal.
 The plan is validated against the proposal and the decision on-chain:
  - the proposal must be APPROVED and its decision finalized (outcome QUARANTINE/PATCH/REVOKE/MONITOR);
  - every action must be either one of the proposal's actions or the action matching the
    winning outcome, and the plan MUST contain the winning outcome's action;
  - the target resource is taken from the proposal (not from the caller).
 Any affected domain (eligible voter) or the proposer - i.e. any domain's DIC - may create the plan,
 so there is no single "DIC" trust anchor.
 A plan has a deadline; if it is not fully verified by then, anyone can escalate it.

@dev Anyone may expire a proposal whose voting never started before the deadline.
     Once voting has started it can only be closed by FederatedVoting.finalizeVoting,
     which removes the expire-vs-finalize race. Expiry escalates the incident.
